{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "103788ed6f7a8201",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "# **27 November 2026 | 2 VWO**\n### Alice in Wonderland | Lesson 3 of 3",
			"x": -360,
			"y": -335,
			"width": 650,
			"height": 80,
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "a1e80a49e0fae25a",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## **Today | 30 minutes**\n**0–3 min**  Polite disagreement (Q1)\n**3–6 min**  Explore the scene\n**6–12 min**  Read + main idea (Q2)\n**12–18 min**  Evidence + linking words (Q3–5)\n**18–22 min**  Vocabulary + false friends (Q6)\n**22–27 min**  Grammar + message starter (Q7–8)\n**27–30 min**  Exit ticket + homework (Q9)",
			"x": -360,
			"y": -225,
			"width": 650,
			"height": 252,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "ca49f910a8ba7115",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "# **Homework**\nWrite **70–90 words** to Alice. Include:\n- **two** correct present perfect forms\n- **two different** modals\n- **three** Chapter 2 health/feelings words\n- **one** linking word\nUnderline these items in your own text.",
			"x": -360,
			"y": 55,
			"width": 650,
			"height": 200,
			"color": "1"
		},
		{
			"id": "6a1e27d8b54e91b9",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## **Class routine**\n1. Follow the text without changing its words.\n2. Work **individually first**, then with your assigned partner.\n3. Use **voice level 0** or **1** as instructed.\n4. When time is up, finish your sentence and listen.",
			"x": -360,
			"y": 281,
			"width": 650,
			"height": 186,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "b30affee541b6f56",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## **Big question**\nWho is being rude at the tea party? What would good advice sound like?",
			"x": 450,
			"y": -335,
			"width": 600,
			"height": 112,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "ace3ccf5a17cdb3b",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## **Learning goals**\n**I can:** read dialogue intensively; copy **one sentence** of advice; find **two** rude actions; explain two meanings of *but*; use grammar and health language in writing.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": -195,
			"width": 600,
			"height": 154,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "664ea0567d570fef",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**0–3 | Starter, silence**\n**Q1:** write **one rule** for being a polite guest or host.\n\n**3–6 | Explore**\nMeet the March Hare and Hatter. Predict who will disagree with Alice.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": -10,
			"width": 600,
			"height": 195,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "124ec56e69fe31fe",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## **TASK before every answer**\n**T** Task: circle the instruction word.\n**A** Answer: letter, phrase or full sentence?\n**S** Special conditions: *exactly*, *copy*, *English*, *two*.\n**K** Keep checking: did you follow **all** instructions?\n\n**Reading focus:** intensive reading and **linking words**.\n**Skills:** evidence, vocabulary, false friends, present perfect and advice.\n**Voice level:** 0 solo work, 1 with partner.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 218,
			"width": 600,
			"height": 230,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "b131bdcfd2bf126e",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## **Original novel | Chapter VII: A Mad Tea-Party**\n*Lewis Carroll, Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland (1865)*\n\n> ‘Have some wine,’ the March Hare said in an encouraging tone.\n\n> Alice looked all round the table, but there was nothing on it but tea. ‘I don't see any wine,’ she remarked.\n\n> ‘There isn't any,’ said the March Hare.\n\n> ‘Then it wasn't very civil of you to offer it,’ said Alice angrily.\n\n> ‘It wasn't very civil of you to sit down without being invited,’ said the March Hare.\n\n> ‘I didn't know it was your table,’ said Alice; ‘it's laid for a great many more than three.’\n\n> ‘Your hair wants cutting,’ said the Hatter. He had been looking at Alice for some time with great curiosity, and this was his first speech.\n\n> ‘You should learn not to make personal remarks,’ Alice said with some severity; ‘it's very rude.’",
			"x": 1140,
			"y": -335,
			"width": 830,
			"height": 705
		},
		{
			"id": "a1e7084cc8139b20",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## **Context and vocabulary support**\nAlice joins the March Hare and Hatter for tea. They disagree about manners and invitations.\n\n**Mini-glossary outside the original:**\n*civil* = beleefd\n*remark* = opmerking\n*invited* = uitgenodigd\n\nCarroll’s original passage is unchanged.",
			"x": 1140,
			"y": 400,
			"width": 830,
			"height": 160,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "23c058c3cec83178",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**6–12 | Read the original conversation**\nFollow the dialogue. Listen for how the speakers treat one another.\n\n**Q2:** choose **A, B or C** for the main idea.",
			"x": 2050,
			"y": -335,
			"width": 630,
			"height": 200,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "042b050b5207a312",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**12–18 | Evidence detectives, pairs**\n**Q3:** copy **EXACTLY ONE sentence** in which Alice gives advice.\n**Q4:** find **TWO** rude actions; explain them in your **own English words**.\n**Q5:** the first *but* means contrast; what does the second *but* mean?",
			"x": 2050,
			"y": -107,
			"width": 630,
			"height": 230,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "67a916c93951ff37",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**18–22 | Read closely**\n**Q6:** Does *civil* mean *polite* or *rude*?\nFind the Dutch meaning of **actual** in a separate teacher example.",
			"x": 2050,
			"y": 151,
			"width": 630,
			"height": 174,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "ec1da702d2b8ed4c",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**22–27 | Language and writing**\n**Q7:** copy **should** from Alice’s words. Complete TWO new present-perfect sentences (*meet*, *offer*).\n**Q8:** write **TWO opening sentences** for a kind message to Alice: one present perfect, one modal.",
			"x": 2050,
			"y": 354,
			"width": 630,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "e61d8f22f7519b75",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**27–30 | Exit ticket: Q9**\nWhat does **exactly one sentence** stop you from doing?\nWrite a clear answer before packing up.",
			"x": 2050,
			"y": 601,
			"width": 630,
			"height": 164,
			"color": "1"
		}
	],
